{
  "id": "10-nyc-parker-pilot",
  "title": "What almost four million New York requests reveal",
  "script_sha256": "4e2b01f01bf6f7706473d17d09a7b28ce6035b6071c9f0bfad2bfa44e853e846",
  "duration": 38.528,
  "beats": [
    {
      "text": "Almost four million New York requests. The biggest category wasn't noise.",
      "scene": "overview",
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.4267,
      "voice_end": 4.2667
    },
    {
      "text": "Illegal parking came first. Six hundred eleven thousand, two hundred eighty two requests.",
      "scene": "parking",
      "start": 4.4267,
      "end": 9.664,
      "voice_end": 9.504
    },
    {
      "text": "I analyzed one year of three one one data. Here is the exact date window.",
      "scene": "query",
      "start": 9.664,
      "end": 14.176,
      "voice_end": 14.016
    },
    {
      "text": "Then I filtered residential noise and grouped the requests by hour.",
      "scene": "noise",
      "start": 14.176,
      "end": 18.0907,
      "voice_end": 17.9307
    },
    {
      "text": "The peak is ten to eleven at night. Sunday has the most requests.",
      "scene": "noise-proof",
      "start": 18.0907,
      "end": 21.9413,
      "voice_end": 21.7813
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat follows a different pattern. Switch the same view to monthly requests.",
      "scene": "heat",
      "start": 21.9413,
      "end": 26.2187,
      "voice_end": 26.0587
    },
    {
      "text": "January is around twenty two times August. And exactly one request was filed under trapping pigeon.",
      "scene": "contrast",
      "start": 26.2187,
      "end": 32.2667,
      "voice_end": 32.1067
    },
    {
      "text": "Requests aren't unique incidents. Keep the queries and results with the chart, so anyone can check the story.",
      "scene": "close",
      "start": 32.2667,
      "end": 38.528,
      "voice_end": 38.368
    }
  ],
